## Outcome

The v2.4 Compiled Native pipeline now retains measured DOM evidence and adds a relationship layer for normal flow, positioned layers, containing blocks, overlap pairs, stacking order, pseudo-elements, and responsive property deltas. A valid Stack/Grid/Flex root is no longer rejected solely because a reconstructable absolute/fixed child exists.

Positioned children are mapped to existing Advanced settings (`position`, horizontal/vertical orientation, responsive X/Y offsets, z-index, and custom width). Grid desktop → one-column mobile transitions use the existing responsive Grid settings; Flex ↔ Grid transitions remain explicit manual decisions because the existing node type cannot switch safely at runtime.

Widget candidates remain evidence-based and editable. Structural wrappers are kept as Container/Grid, while Icon Box/Image Box/composite candidates use nested members without duplicate mapping rows. Registered candidates with score `>= 0.60` are preselected.

## Asset and residual-style behavior

Local package assets receive stable `mappingId`, safe `sourcePath`, availability, and nullable `targetUrl`; filesystem paths are removed before the browser response. The target preview exposes explicit Local asset mapping inputs and does not upload or persist files during analysis. Unresolved Image/Image Box and local background assets remain visible as `pendingAssets` warnings, while partial Apply uses the registered empty-image state and complete visual finalization still requires a safe persistent URL.

Native-safe style is applied to Canvas settings. Unsupported-but-safe residuals produce scoped CSS patches as review notes. Custom JavaScript is not used for layout or CSS fallback. Transform/overlap ambiguity, missing layout evidence, unsupported mode transitions, and missing widget mappings remain blocking with source/viewport remediation; unresolved assets are warnings for partial Apply.

