## Partial asset Apply — 2026-08-30

The approved workflow now permits an explicit partial Apply when the only remaining asset findings are unresolved local images or local CSS background images. The target report retains each item in `assetWarnings` and `pendingAssets` with `blocking: false`, exposes `canApplyComplete: false`, and changes the action label to `Apply partial · N asset(s) pending`. Structural blockers and incomplete widget mapping still prevent Apply. Image and Image Box nodes receive an empty-image placeholder through their existing v2.4 widget contracts; raw local filesystem paths are never sent to Canvas.

## Runtime blank-screen regression

Chrome read-only reload reproduced the reported failure as:

`Uncaught (in promise) SyntaxError: Invalid regular expression: /^(?:https?:|/: Unterminated group`

The cause was the `/` escape inside the outer JavaScript template literal. JavaScript removed the escape before Vue compiled the target-stage template, leaving an invalid regular expression in the `v-if` expression. The fix moves residual-CSS and local-asset filtering into setup-level computed values (`automaticCompiledNativeReviewCssNotes` and `automaticCompiledNativeLocalAssets`); the template now only reads their lengths/items. A fresh Chrome reload returned the full editor DOM and produced no new error entry. The previous `automaticCompiledNativeSourceBlockCount` error remains only as historical console-buffer evidence from an earlier session.

